# Every text file is LF in the repository and LF in the working tree. The first half was
# already true, but only because core.autocrlf happened to be set on one machine — a
# contributor without it commits CRLF and no gate here notices, because terraform fmt, ruff
# and checkov all tolerate either. This makes it a property of the repository instead.
#
# eol=lf rather than a bare text=auto is the half that stops the warnings: without it Git
# keeps rewriting these files to CRLF on checkout and back to LF on commit. Nothing in this
# repository needs CRLF, and there are no binary files for text=auto to misclassify.
* text=auto eol=lf
